{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788510238-H3AcmPHd0j3BxlxFX0ll","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Implemented. You can now pass `enable_state=False` when creating your app:\n\n```python\napp = rx.App(enable_state=False)   # fully stateless\napp = rx.App()                     # default: state enabled\n```\n\n## What changed\n\n**`reflex/app.py`**\n- Added `enable_state: bool = True` field to `App` (reflex/app.py:404).\n- `__post_init__` now calls `_enable_state()` only when `enable_state` is true — otherwise no state class is assigned, no state manager is created, and no Socket.IO/event namespace is mounted (reflex/app.py:486).\n- `_enable_state()` always runs `_setup_state()` after assigning `State`, so state setup is consistent whether it happens at init or later.\n- Removed all automatic state enabling: `_compile_page` no longer enables state based on compiled content, and the backend-only compile path no longer calls `_enable_state()` when replaying stateful pages.\n\n**`reflex/compiler/compiler.py`**\n- Deleted the page-content analysis from `compile_unevaluated_page` (the `on_load` / `_has_stateful_event_triggers` / var-data scan) — it now returns just the `Component`, treating every page as stateless regardless of content.\n- Dropped the `state` parameter from `compile_page` / `_compile_page` / `ExecutorSafeFunctions` plumbing, so pages are compiled with no `state_name` and no state assumptions.\n\n**Behavior when disabled:** pages with `on_load`, stateful event triggers, or even direct state-var references compile and run without state support — nothing is auto-enabled. State-dependent wraps (overlay/connection banner) and the stateful `on_error` handler are skipped. The one guard that remains is the existing compile-time `ReflexRuntimeError` for components that genuinely render `rx.State` vars — that's intentional, since compiling those stateless would reproduce the exact `TypeError: can't access property '$$typeof', Context is undefined` crash you're trying to avoid (a dangling `useContext(StateContexts.…)` pointing at an empty contexts file).\n\n**Note:** this also fixes the underlying bug for stateful apps — implicit detection is gone entirely, so state is set up upfront instead of being discovered mid-compile (after some state-context consumers had already been emitted).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `tests/units`: **3298 passed, 34 skipped**; `tests/benchmarks/test_compilation.py`: 6 passed.\n- End-to-end script: `App(enable_state=False)` → `_state`/`_state_manager`/`sio` all `None`; pages with `on_load` and a state-var reference compiled stateless; full `_compile(dry_run=True)` succeeded; default `App()` still fully stateful.\n- Updated tests: `test_app_state_determination` now asserts state is enabled by default and `None` with `enable_state=False`; the stateless playwright/tailwind integration apps set the flag explicitly; expected-output tests updated for stateful-by-default wraps.\n\nSources: [Reflex PR #5583 — disable stateful app detection](https://github.com/reflex-dev/reflex/pull/5583), [v0.8.3 release notes](https://newreleases.io/project/github/reflex-dev/reflex/release/v0.8.3), [App API reference](https://reflex.dev/docs/api-reference/app/)","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Z.AI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7764e7ad-7165-4849-a6ff-d2cf0980932e","uuid":"ad40b07b-675f-4257-99fe-63f75828dbfc","timestamp":"2026-09-04T08:24:20.992Z","request_id":"gen-1788510238-H3AcmPHd0j3BxlxFX0ll"}
